Cooperation Article 22 In carrying out the handling of child victims of acts of violence as referred to in Article 18, the Regional Government may conduct cooperation with: a. vertical agencies;
b. provincial government;
c. other district/city governments;
d. village/sub-district government;
e. non-governmental organizations;
f. private parties;
g. the community; and/or
h. families.
Article 23 (1) In certain circumstances the Regional Government may conduct cooperation with: a. other Regional Governments;
b. police;
