The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in (2) paragraph (1). include: a. establishing, implementing policies, programs, and conducting cooperation activities in the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
b. facilitating the establishment of institutional protection for women and children from acts of violence and providing support for facilities and infrastructure; c. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence in accordance with the financial capacity of the Region; d. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. providing protection services for women and children victims of acts of violence;
f. encouraging and increasing community participation; and
g. appointing parents and/or substitute family caregivers as a protective measure for children who are victims of acts of violence.
